  "decision_conditions": [
    "This consent is valid for two years.\rReason: In order that the nature of work pertaining to this consent remains appropriate.\r",
    "The works hereby approved shall be carried out as closely as possible in accordance with British Standard 3998 [2010] 'Tree Works' and shall not exceed the previous pruning points. Care shall be taken to retain as much leaf bearing structure as possible. The works shall not include any thinning of growth within the crown.\rReason: In the interests of the health, safety and appearance of the preserved tree.\r",
    "Tree work should not be carried out during periods that are likely to interfere with or disturb breeding birds or mammals.\rReason: In order to comply with the requirements of the Wildlife and Countryside Act (1981) and Conservation of Habitats and Species Regulations (2010).\r",
    "The Council does not consider that the grounds specified by the applicant/agent (i.e. increased exposure) sufficient reason to justify the proposed heavy crown reduction of a mature and prominent tree, would have a significantly negative impact upon the tree's long-term health, and the tree's amenity value which makes a positive contribution to the amenity of the locality and wider borough."
